---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="What The Trend Times collects when you read the site, email us, or join a list, and how advertising cookies will work once ads begin."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-11-04')}
	updatedDate={new Date('2026-11-26')}
	eyebrow="PRIVACY POLICY"
	author="Jaewon Oh"
	showDate={false}
>
	<p>
		This policy covers thetrendtimes.com ("the site"), published by Jaewon Oh ("we", "us"), an
		individual based in South Korea. It explains what data we collect, why we hold it, and the choices
		you have. Questions go to <a href="mailto:contact@thetrendtimes.com">contact@thetrendtimes.com</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Server and security logs.</strong> The site runs on Cloudflare. When you load a page,
			Cloudflare processes your IP address, browser type, and the page you requested to deliver the
			site and to block abuse. Cloudflare may also set a security cookie, such as __cf_bm, to tell a
			person apart from a bot. See the
			<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Aggregate traffic measurement.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page
			views. It runs without cookies and does not follow you to other sites.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Fonts.</strong> Pages load fonts from Google Fonts, so your browser sends your IP address
			to Google when fetching them.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Email you send us.</strong> If you email us, we keep your address and message so we can
			reply. If you join the newsletter, we keep your address in our database until you unsubscribe.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Early-access list.</strong> If you join the DocChase waitlist on
			<a href="/tools/docchase/">/tools/docchase/</a>, we store the email address you enter, with the
			product name, in our database. The receipt reminder demo on that page runs in your browser and
			sends us nothing.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not sell personal data. We do not ask for accounts or passwords, and we do not collect payment
		details.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
	<p>
		The site does not show ads today and does not set advertising cookies. When we begin to serve ads
		through Google AdSense, third-party vendors, including Google, will use cookies to serve ads based
		on your prior visits to this site and other sites. Google's use of advertising cookies lets it and
		its partners serve ads to you based on those visits.
	</p>
	<p>
		For visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland, we will ask for
		your consent through a consent management platform certified by Google before any advertising
		cookie is set. If you decline, you may see non-personalized or limited ads.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Turn off personalized ads in
			<a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google My Ad Center</a>.
		</li>
		<li>
			Opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at
			<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
		</li>
		<li>
			Google explains how it uses data from partner sites in
			<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.
		</li>
		<li>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Legal bases</h2>
	<p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we rely on these bases:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Legitimate interests.</strong> Server and security logs, and aggregate measurement, so the
			site stays online and readable.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Consent.</strong> Newsletter and early-access emails, and advertising cookies once ads
			begin. You can withdraw consent at any time.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Steps you ask for.</strong> Answering an email you send us.</li>
		<li><strong>Legal obligation.</strong> Keeping records where the law requires it.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>You can object to processing based on legitimate interests by writing to us.</p>

	<h2>How long we keep data</h2>
	<p>
		Email correspondence stays for as long as we need it to answer you and for our records. Newsletter
		and early-access addresses stay until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them. Cloudflare and
		Google keep their own logs under their own policies.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		You can ask what personal data we hold about you, and ask us to correct, delete, restrict, or
		export it, or to stop processing it. You can also withdraw consent you gave earlier. Email
		<a href="mailto:contact@thetrendtimes.com?subject=Privacy%20request">contact@thetrendtimes.com</a>
		with the subject line "Privacy request". We aim to answer within 30 days.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can complain to your local data protection authority. In South Korea that is the Personal
		Information Protection Commission.
	</p>

	<h2>California residents</h2>
	<p>
		We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-site behavioral advertising
		while the site runs without personalized ads. If that changes, we will update this policy and give
		you the opt-out the law requires. California residents can ask to know, correct, or delete personal
		information by emailing contact@thetrendtimes.com. We will not discriminate against you for using
		these rights.
	</p>

	<h2>Children</h2>
	<p>The site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>When we change this policy, we update the date at the top of this page.</p>
</Layout>
